## Non-Mermaid description (accessible alternative)

The frozen R1 benchmark supplies a calibrated failure hazard and cause
belief to a budget-aware controller. The controller selects among verify,
continue, recover, escalate, abstain, and terminate, each with a declared
cost and postconditions. Every selected action is followed by independent
adjudication that checks execution fidelity, fault removal, downstream
state consistency, scientific validity, and verifier independence. Accepted
transitions become verified intervention records that build immutable
process-supervised training views. The trained policies are evaluated on
unseen-fault recovery and clean-task regression gates. Hidden fault truth is
never consumed by the controller.
